    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1d3623eb",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts three children in a science class, engaged in a chemistry experiment with a blue chemical reaction. The overlaid text reads, 'when i grew up i want to be a gas plumber.' The intent is to create a humorous juxtaposition between the children's innocent, enthusiastic scientific exploration and the adult profession of a 'gas plumber,' which is a real job. The humor stems from the absurdity of a child's aspiration being tied to a profession that is both mundane and potentially dangerous. There is no toxicity present in the image or text. The meme is not abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. It is a lighthearted, non-harmful joke that relies on the contrast between childhood innocence and adult occupational reality. The children in the image are diverse in appearance, but no harmful stereotypes or discriminatory tropes are present or implied. The meme's purpose is purely comedic and does not target any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7df1e3ec"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
